// §2 Definition. The answer-target block for the focus keyword and the
// first place the phrase appears in body copy. Paragraph two does the
// synonym work ("vacancy clean", "exit clean", "bond clean", "make-ready")
// so one page answers all of them.
//
// ⚠️ Paragraph two draws the bond-clean line at /end-of-lease-cleaning/ ON
// PURPOSE, rather than competing with it. That page is built, it is aimed at
// tenants AND agencies (its own §3 has cards for both), and its card 2
// already sends property managers here. Two pages both trying to own "bond
// clean" would split the term between them.
const definitionBody: TextBlockBody[] = [
  'Real estate cleaning is the cleaning a managing agency arranges rather than a tenant: vacancy cleans between tenancies, exit cleans measured against an outgoing condition report, and routine cleans on the properties an agency looks after. TLB Cleaning works with agencies and property managers across the Northern Rivers, the Tweed and the Southern Gold Coast.',
  'A vacancy clean, an exit clean, a make-ready and a bond clean are close relatives with different payers. If you are a tenant cleaning your own place before the final inspection, the page you want is end of lease and bond cleaning. This page is for the person who has a vacancy on the board, a landlord asking when it will be listed, and no interest in ringing four cleaners to find out who is free.',
];

